# ir_emitter_core.pith — the lowering engine
#
# turns a checked ast into text ir. this module owns the parts of
# lowering that are mutually recursive by nature and share the
# per-function state below: expressions, statements, ownership
# (retain/release insertion), and the function lifecycle around them.
#
# everything else lives in a named satellite and is imported here:
#
#   ir_builder          the output buffer, registers, labels, strings,
#                       and the current function's variable maps
#   ir_call_emit        call and label instruction wrappers
#   ir_alias_registry   names that stand for other names: type and
#                       module aliases, import renames, global kinds
#   ir_struct_registry  struct and enum shapes
#   ir_method_tables    method symbols and return kinds
#   ir_generics         generic declarations and specializations
#   ir_decode_emit      json / toml / config decode-call emission
#   ir_match_emit       match lowering
#
# the satellites never import this module back. where one needs an
# expression or a block emitted in place, it takes the emitter as an
# explicit fn-value parameter (emit_expr, emit_block, ...) — grep for
# those names to see every seam.
#
# two type vocabularies meet here. the checker speaks tids (integer
# type ids, TID_INT and friends); emission speaks kind strings
# ("int", "string", "map_str_val", ...) that pick runtime calls and
# retain/release behavior. ir_type_from_tid and ir_retkind translate.
#
# a function compiles in one pass: ir_emit_fn resets the per-function
# state, emits the header and parameters, walks the body once
# (ir_block -> ir_stmt -> ir_expr), then closes with cleanup and a
# default return. deferred lambda bodies emit after the function that
# captured them.
#
# the ir instruction format itself is documented where it is consumed:
# cranelift/codegen/src/ir_consumer.rs.

